hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"945","Abdullah bin Saeed Al-Ashjaj and Muhammad bin Hisham told us, they said: Ibn Idris told us, and Ali bin Khashram told us, Abd told us By God, he means Ibn Idris. Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Ammar, H, and Ya’qub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi told us, H, and I read it on Bundar, that Yahya told them, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, Abdul Rahman bin Abdullah bin Abi Ammar told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Babih, on the authority of Ya’la bin Umayyah, who said: I said to Omar bin Al-Khattab, may God Almighty be pleased with him: I am amazed at the people’s shortening of prayer, and he said God Almighty: There is no blame on you if you shorten the prayer if you fear that those who disbelieve will test you. Surat An-Nisa, verse 101, and this has been mentioned, so Omar said May God Almighty be pleased with him: I was amazed at what I was amazed at, so I mentioned that to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: “It is charity given to God in charity.” It is upon you, so accept his charity.” This is the hadith of Bundar."
